                    caption: "Transthoracic echocardiogram before TAvI. Panel A:. Apical four-chamber view at end-diastole. The septum has a sigmoid contour. Panel B: Apical four-chamber view at end-systole. There is near cavitary obliteration at the mid-ventricular. level. Panel C: Continuous wave Doppler interrogation across. the mid-ventricular obstruction. There is E to A reversal which  is consistent with grade 1 diastolic dysfunction. There is a late peaking gradient across the mid-ventricular obstruction with a. peak velocity of 1.7 m sec-1 which gives a gradient of 12 mm. Hg. Panel D: Continuous wave Doppler interrogation across the. aortic valve. The peak velocity was 5.5 m sec-1. Peak gradient. was 121 mm Hg and mean gradient was 83 mm Hg."
