                    caption: "A: Preprocedural computed tomography (CT) image (arrow). D: CT image on postprocedural day 25: the false of the aortic complex (double oblique coronal section): a nar- Iumen of the dissection became thrombolized and diminished. row and heavily calcified sinotubular junction (STJ), and bulky (arrow). E: Intraprocedural angiography of transcatheter heart calcification on the aortic valve cusps. B: Preprocedural CT valve (THv) deployment: outward displacement of the calcified image of the STJ (a = 20.1 mm; b = 19.2 mm): a narrow and nodule on the STJ (arrow). F: Intraprocedural angiography afheavily calcified STJ. C: CT image on postprocedural day 3: a ter THv implantation: \"double shadow\" of the dissected limited dissection of an ascending aorta with STJ entry ascending aorta (three arrows)."
