        title: "Reversible thrombotic aortic valve restenosis after valve-in-valve transcatheter aortic valve replacement",
        source: "CATHETERIZATION AND CARDIOVASCULAR INTERVENTIONS",
        author: "Patrick J Goleski, Mark Reisman, Creighton W Don",
        abstract: "Thrombotic aortic valve restenosis following transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR) has not been extensively reported and the rates of TAVR valve thrombosis are not known. We present three cases of valve-in-valve (VIV) restenosis following TAVR with the balloon expandable transcatheter heart valves, presumably due to valve thrombosis that improved with anticoagulation. © 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
