                    caption: "Hemodynamics at baseline and following transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR). (A). Baseline hemodynamics. 1. Elevated left ventricular end diastolic pressure (40mmHg). 2. Delayed upstroke in aortic pressure tracing. 3. Maximum gradient across the aortic valve of 80 mmHg. 4. Mean gradient across the aortic valve of 40 mmHg. 5. Low aortic end diastolic pressure (60 mmHg), with equalization of left ventricular end diastolic and aortic diastolic pressures. (B) Hemodynamics following TAVR. 1. Mildly increased left ventricular end-diastolic pressure (30 mmHg) that is significantly Iower than baseline (40 mmHg). 2. Normal upstroke in aortic pressure tracing. 3. and 4. Minimal gradients across the aortic valve. 5. Normal aortic diastolic pressure (100 mmHg) that is significantly higher than baseline (60 mmHg) [Color figure can be viewed at wileyonlinelibrary.com]"
