                    caption: "Panels (a) and (b): Continuous wave Doppler through the LVOT demonstrating a late-peaking dagger-shaped signal and peak to peak maximal instantaneous gradient of 101 mmHg, along with mean aortic valve gradient of 40 mmHg. Panel (c): Invasive hemodynamic tracings demonstrating a resting gradient from the left ventricle to aorta of 55 mmHg, which increases to over 150 mmHg on post-PVC beats along with. appearance of a spike-and-dome aortic waveform and decrease in the aortic pulse-pressure post-PVC. Panel (d): Post-procedural invasive. hemodynamic tracings demonstrating a residual resting mean aortic valve gradient of 22 mmHg, a delayed aortic pressure uprise, and no change noted post-PVC consistent with moderate aortic valve stenosis [Color figure can be viewed at wileyonlinelibrary.com]"
