                    caption: "u RE 3 Critical steps for implantation of the Edwards Ultra valve via the right axillary route using a Lunderquist wire (Cook Medical, USA). (a) Aortogram demonstrating annular plane (arrow). (b) The delivery sheath introducer is advanced across the aortic valve into the left ventricle. (c) This allows the sheath to be advanced across the valve (star icon) with the sheath transition point being intraarterial. (d) The valve is inserted into the ascending aorta. The valve is premounted on the expansion balloon, marked by the radio-opaque dot. By pulling back the sheath, the valve is uncovered fully. (e) The stent valve is pushed into deployment position; poor coaxiality is demonstrated here. (f) The stent valve is deployed into an optimal position [Color figure can be viewed at wileyonlinelibrary.com]"
