                    caption: "(a) Heavily calcified type I bicuspid aortic valve. (b) Final angiogram following transcatheter aortic valve replacement with the Evolut PRO valve, showing a correctly implanted valve and no signs of a pseudoaneurysm (contrast extravasation) yet. (c, d) Multi-slice computed tomography images showing left coronary sinus perforation with a pseudoaneurysm (red arrow) in multiplanar reconstruction (MPR) and 3Dvolume rendering views. Also, notice the oval-shaped transcatheter heart valve stent frame at the level of the calcified leaflets in this bicuspid aortic valve. (e, f) Multi-slice computed tomography at 1 month of follow-up showing thrombosis of the pseudoaneurysm (white arrow) in MPR view and obliteration of the cavity in the 3D-volume rendering view. LCC, left coronary cusp; NCC, non-coronary cusp; RCC, right coronary cusp [Color figure can be viewed at wileyonlinelibrary.com]"
