                    caption: "Applying CT-predicted valve plane to fluoroscopic imaging: (A) zoomed image of aortic root from 16 LAO and 6 cranial, showing that the most caudal portion of each coronary sinus occurs approximately on the same line; (B) the same image shown in 2D on CT with the valve plane identified by a broken line; and (C) fluoroscopic image in 16 LAO, 6 cranial. with the DFM valve in the left ventricle. Based on the CT images, an imaginary line is drawn from the bottom of the pigtail catheter in the NCC to the LCC using the same angulation. identified on the CT images. This imaginary line is the target for positioning the ventricular ring of the DFM valve.."
