                    caption: "Schematic representation of the valve plane normal vector as determined by the tilt angles (i.e., rotations to the original coordinate system) used to obtain the double-oblique view of the valve plane. The ellipse shows the valve plane orientation and the bold blue. arrow is the normal vector. The black arrows in the plane are examples of included C-arm projections. From the coronal view, the orthogonal axes are titled by angle  to intersect. with the bottom of the left and non-coronary cusps. Then, from the left view, the axes are. rotated by angle  to intersect with the right coronary cusp, thus bringing the transverse view into the valve plane."
