                    caption: "Echocardiographic evaluation of the aortic valve. (a) TEE showed a floating mass attached to the ventricular aspect of the aortic valve (red arrow). The aortic valve had a massive. regurgitation secondary to left coronary cusp fracture (b). Intra procedural TEE showed the correct function of the aortic prosthesis with normal gradients and no paravalvular regurgitation (c and d); 2-month follow-up transthoracic echocardiography confirmed the correct function of the valve (e and f).."
