                    caption: "Transthoracic echocardiography (TTE) of the patient 3 weeks after TAVI procedure. TTE long-axis view with colour-flow Doppler signal showing a left-to-right shunt (white arrow) initiating in the aorta behind the valved stent and directed toward the infundibulum of the right ventricle. A small pericardial effusion (white stars). and a moderate dilatation of the right ventricle were associated. Ao, ascending aorta; LA, left atrium; LV, left ventricle; RV, right ventricle."
