                    caption: "Case 1: Panel A - 3D MDCT reconstruction of the aorta and iliofemoral vessels demonstrating severely tortuous iliac arteries; Panel B - Frontal plane angiographic image showing severe persistent iliac tortuosity despite placement of bilateral stiff 0.035\" guidewires; Panel C - Frontal plane angiographic image during placement of a left-sided 16F vascular sheath with visible sheath malformation due to tortuosity; Panel D - Annular plane angiographic image during contrast aortography demonstrating appropriate deployment of the aortic prosthesis; Panel E - Marked disruption of the access sheath after removal with the dislocated portion of the balloon lodged within the sheath (inset). MDCT = Multi-detector computed tomography"
