                    caption: "Echocardiographic and multidetector computed tomography (MDCT) images of bicuspid aortic valve. Sievers' type 1 bicuspid aortic valve with raphe between right and left coronary cusps (asterisk) was observed in 2-dimensional (A) and 3-dimensional transesophageal echocardiography (B) as well as MDCT (C). Aortic annulus dimension was measured at the virtual basal ring (D). The Sapien 3 valve was positioned within the aortic annulus (E) and deployed with balloon inflation (F). Postprocedural. MDCT showed the expansion of the Sapien 3 valve at sinus of Valsalva (G) and annulus (H). Green, red and yellow dots indicate hinge points at the right-, left- and non-coronary cups, respectively.e"
