                    caption: "(A) Final TAVI result, showing a good position of the MCV prosthesis with no paravalvular regurgitation on aortography. (B) The 6 F compatible snare (from the left sided 18 F sheath) has grabbed (arrow) the 0.035\" standard wire (that was advanced in the abdominal aorta through the right sided 6 F sheath). (C) The 0.035\" wire is dragged into the 18 F sheath and externalized. Consequently a peripheral over-the-wire 7.0/40 mm balloon is easily advanced from the right femoral/iliac artery to the left in a cross-over fashion. (D) Final result of the 18 F puncture site closure (arrow) through the peripheral balloon (black arrow), showing complete and uncomplicated hemostasis."
