        abstract: "Sinus contrast material retention after transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR) is a rare phenomenon that may reflect an increased risk for thrombotic complications. We present 3 cases of persistent contrast agent retention in the sinus of Valsalva during the TAVR procedure that portend the occurrence of embolic stroke or bioprosthetic valve thrombosis. (Level of Difficulty: Advanced.).",
