                    caption: "central apneas, the movements of the thorax and abdomen were absent. Duration from the onset of the first breath terminating the apnea to the nadir of the subsequent dip in the SO2 measured at the finger indicates the LFCT, which is considerably long (an average of 10 consecutive apnea-hyperpnea cycles during the first episode of stage 2 sleep, 26 s). (B) Follow-up polysomnography performed 7 months after TAVI. Five occurrences of obstructive apnea were detected. During Fig. 1. obstructive apneas, the out-of-phase movements of the thorax and abdomen were observed. LFCT was shorter than that before TAvI (an average of 10 consecutive apnea-hyperpnea cycles during the first episode of stage 2 sleep, 17 s). TAVI, transcatheter aortic valve implantation; EEG, electroencephalogram; EOG, electro-oculogram; EMG, submental electromyogram; ECG, electrocardiography; SO2, oxyhemoglobin saturation; LFCT, lung-to-finger circulation time."
