        title: "Intravenous Thrombolysis and Mechanical Thrombectomy in Patients with Stroke after TAVI: A Report of Two Cases",
        source: "JOURNAL OF STROKE & CEREBROVASCULAR DISEASES",
        author: "Lucio D'Anna, Ozan Demir, Soma Banerjee, Iqbal Malik",
        abstract: "Transcatheter Aortic Valve Implantation (TAVI) is an increasingly treatment modality for severe aortic stenosis, which is associated with a considerable peri-procedural risk of stroke. To date, the clinical safety and efficacy of Tissue plasminogen activator (tPA) and mechanical thrombectomy in stroke post-TAVI is not established. We describe 2 cases of patients with stroke after TAVI who received tPA therapy and mechanical thrombectomy.",
