                    caption: "Patient 3: Use of the commissure tab on the Evolut PRO+ transcatheter heart valve to visualize the appropriate location via which to engage the coronary ostia. White circles indicate. the commissural tab (C-tab) (A-H). (C, E, and G) Perpendicular images. (D, F, and H) Right-anterior-oblique cranial en face shortaxis images (right-anterior-oblique 74, cranial 48). From the commissure tab position, a virtual triangle was constructed to indicate the location of three commissure positions on the shortaxis image (D). By avoiding the apex of the virtual triangle, engaging the coronary ostia became much easier and enabled right. (E and F) and left (G and H) coronary angiography using 5Fr JR4 and JL4 diagnostic catheters from the left radial artery."
