        author: "Joanna Bartkowiak, Vratika Agarwal, Mark Lebehn, Tamim M Nazif, Isaac George, Susheel K Kodali, Torsten P Vahl, Rebecca T Hahn",
        abstract: "Background: Limited data exist on strain changes after transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) in patients with aortic regurgitation (AR). Case summary: Three patients with AR undergoing TAVI showed an initial reduction in global longitudinal strain (GLS), followed by sustained GLS improvement within the first year. Discussion: Findings align with those of surgically treated patients with AR. There is a possible superiority of GLS to left ventricular end-diastolic diameter ratio in assessing patients with severe volume overload.",
