        pmid: "22645293",
        title: "Transcatheter aortic valve implantation in situs inversus totalis",
        source: "INTERACTIVE CARDIOVASCULAR AND THORACIC SURGERY",
        author: "Christophe L Dubois, Paul Herijgers",
        abstract: "A frail 84-year old lady with situs inversus totalis and symptomatic aortic stenosis underwent a successful transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI) after extensive diagnostic work-up. We show illustrative pre- and postintervention three-dimensional reconstruction imaging and describe how conventional and dedicated imaging software can support the planning and performance of TAVI.",
        keywords: null,
        year: 2012,
        Basic_Info: {
            Age: "84",
            Gender: "Female",
            Case: "Situs inversus totalis and symptomatic aortic stenosis",
            Previous_History: "N/A"
        },
        Pre_Info: {
            Mean_Gradient: "75 mmHg",
            Peak_Gradients: "N/A",
            Valve_Area: "N/A",
            Maximum_Velocity: "N/A",
            Ejection_Fraction: "N/A"
        },
        Procedure: {
            Valve_Diameter: "26 mm",
            Valve_Type: "Edwards SAPIEN"
        },
        Result: {
            Death: false,
            Paravalvular_Leak: false,
            Mean_Gradient: "N/A",
            Peak_Gradients: "N/A",
            Valve_Area: "N/A",
            Maximum_Velocity: "N/A"
        },
        Files: {
            PDF: "D:/Romy/SAIRI/TAVI/Code/pdf_downloads/10.1093_icvts_ivs227.pdf",
            Images: [
                {
                    path: "D:/Romy/SAIRI/TAVI/Code/extract_downloads/10.1093_icvts_ivs227/images/8cf8c0f2b036163afa955e478f88ee6aa9f8cbbd93d3142b94d01d3df1022b2e.jpg",
                    caption: ": Three-dimensional reconstruction of a preoperative cardiac angio-CT in antero-posterior and slightly caudal projection shows an inverted (rightward) orientation of the ventricle apex (arrow) as well as the great vessels (a). A postimplantation aortic angiography (b) confirms the correct position of the valved stent (dark frame) with the proximal stent edge slightly protruding into the left ventricular outflow tract, hereby nicely covering the annulus of the native valve (arrowheads), while still ensuring coronary flow (/*right coronary artery and /*/*left coronary artery). Post-processing of a postoperative CT with the dedicated software shows the position and orientation of the SAPIEN valve in situs inversus (c). The double-oblique vessel view with volume rendering (d) confirms the exact position of the valve prosthesis at the level of the annulus (arrowheads). Ao: aorta; LA: left atrium; LV: left ventricle; PA: pulmonary artery."
                }
            ]
        },
