                    caption: "Three-dimensional measurement of aortic annular calcification by real time 3D transesophageal echocardiography (RT3DTEE). A, C, E. Left-sided green panels are long-axis images of aortic valve, which is described in green line in B, D, and F, respectively. B, D, F. Right-sided green panels are. short-axis images at basal aortic annular ring. A and C are images which is cutting along the calcification at NCC and LCC. Calcification protruding into LVOT at NCC area is longi-. tudinally continuing of 14.7 mm (arrow, A) and protruding inward of 5.2 mm at annular plane (arrow, B). Calcification at LCC and RCC area is protruding inward of 2.5 mm and of 1.7 mm at annular plane, respectively (arrow, C and D). The. gap between 2 protruding calcification at NCC and LCC is 7.8 mm (D). At basal annular ring, the annular diameter and area are 20.1 x 25.7 mm and 409 mm2 (F). RCC = right coronary cusp; NCC = noncoronary cusp; LVOT = left ventricular outflow tract; LCC = left coronary cusp.."
