                    caption: "Paravalvular regurgitation (PVR) after transcatheter aortic valve replacement (TAVR) and regurgitant orifice by real time. three-dimensional transesophageal echocardiography (RT3DTEE). A, B. show long- and short-axis view for PVR after the prosthesis. deployment. Trivial transvalvular regurgitation is observed near a wire (arrow, A). At short-axis view, cross-sectional area and diameter of vena contracta are 0.11 cm? and 7.8 x 2.0 mm, which is considered as moderate degree (B). C. shows the regurgitant ori-. fice. VC = vena contracta."
