                    caption: "A. 2D transthoracic echocardiography (2DTTE): parasternal long-axis view shows the presence of a large ventricular septal defect (VSD) just below the ventricular side of the prosthesis (white arrow) and two pseudoaneurysmal cavities on right ventricular side. B. 2D transthoracic echocardiography (2DTTE): color Doppler displays the passage of blood flow through the VDS toward the two pseudoaneurysmal cavities (black arrow). C. 2D transesophageal echocardiography (2DTEE): in mid-esophageal longitudinal 38 view, color Doppler allows the visualization of the blood flow through the first pseudoaneurysm (black arrow); the second cavity located in the far-field scan is no longer detectable. Ao = aorta; LV = left ventricle; I = first pseudoaneurysmal cavity; II = second pseudoaneurysmal cavity; LA = left atrium; RA = right atrium; RV = right ventricle"
