                    caption: "Echocardiographic findings in patient 1: a Preoperative 3-D TEE at peak systole showing a severely stenotic aortic valve. b On. TTE the Doppler peak pressure gradient is 89 mm Hg with a mean. pressure gradient of 60 mm Hg. c Before TAVI, TEE demonstrates a chronic dissection flap (arrow) involving the ascending aorta be-.  ginning just distal to the Dacron graft. After the procedure, TTE demonstrates a normal opening of the newly implanted aortic valve (d) with a peak transaortic gradient of 27 mm Hg and a mean gradient of 12 mm Hg (e). Ao = Aorta; FL = false lumen."
