                    caption: "J-Valve implantation in a patient with high risk of coronary obstruction. Upper Panel: Note both left and right coronary height was all less than 10 mm with narrow aortic sinus (a-d). Lower Panel: Angiogram also revealed low coronary ostium height (e). Valve deployment process (f-h): Three Clasper were released and pushed back gently into the aortic sinuses, the valve was retrieved into the annular plan with the help of the locking device. The valve was then deployed without rapid ventricular pacing, further angiogram confirmed good position of the valve while without obvious paravalvular leakage"
