                    caption: "A: Annular measurement by cardiac computed tomography scan. The aortic annular size was 17.7 mm in area and 17.9 mm in circumference. B: Three-dimensional CT scan showing the relationship between the thoracotomy. and the aortic root, and the difference between the thoracotomies. MIAVR is usually performed from the third intercostal space, so that the aortic valve, the aortotomy and the thoracotomy are located along a straight line. However, in the present case, surgery was performed through a right anterolateral thoracotomy at the fourth intercostal space in consideration of the access to the aortic root. AV indicates aortic valve.."
