                    caption: "(A) Cine image and (B) intracardiac echocardiography during inflation of the Inoue balloon catheter. Percutaneous antegrade balloon aortic valvuloplasty was performed using a 26-mm Inoue balloon under intracardiac echocardiography guide. The blue arrowhead and blue dotted line indicate the inflated Inoue balloon catheter. The yellow dotted line indicates the aortic valve (AV). (C) Polygraph recording before and (D) after valvuloplasty. The AV peak pressure gradient improved from 45 mmHg to 12 mmHg."
