                    caption: "Chest CT [mediastinal window, axial view (A), coronal view (B)] showing porcelain aorta and hostile thorax caused by radiation therapy. (C) 3D image of the aorta showing heavy calcification in the ascending aorta. (D) Short-axis view of the aortic valve. All three cusps are severely calcified,. especially in the non-coronary cusp. (E) A self-expandable valve is suitable for the icicle calcification. in the left ventricular outflow tract. Residual aortic regurgitation is also attributable to the calcifica-. tion."
