        source: "FRONTIERS IN CARDIOVASCULAR MEDICINE",
        author: "Elsa Hebbo #, Alessandro El Khoury, Dounia Iskandarani, Fadi Sawaya",
        abstract: "We describe a case of valve thrombosis and a subsequent thromboembolic event within only 10 days of transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI). Postprocedural anticoagulants are not standard of care medications post-TAVI in patients without atrial fibrillation. Valve thrombosis is an indication to initiate anticoagulation to resolve and prevent further thrombus.",
