        title: "Case Report: Double chimney in valve-in-valve procedures for high-risk coronary obstruction",
        source: "FRONTIERS IN CARDIOVASCULAR MEDICINE",
        author: "Selma T Cook, Mario Togni, Stéphane Cook",
        abstract: "The chimney technique has been utilized to minimize the risk of coronary artery obstruction during valve-in-valve procedures. Here, we present a case involving an 89-year-old female patient with low coronary ostia, severe aortic regurgitation, and intractable heart decompensation caused by degenerated aortic bioprosthesis. The patient underwent a successful transcatheter aortic valve implantation procedure using the chimney technique in both coronary ostia.",
        keywords: "VIVID classification; chimney technique; coronary artery obstruction (CAO); transcatheter aortic valve implantation (TAVI); valve-in valve.",
