                    caption: "Transthoracic and transesophageal echocardiography (TEE) images of the aortic valve at the time of diagnosis of infective endocarditis. A: Parasternal long-axis images of the mitral valve. Significant mitral regurgitation can be seen just beneath the strut of the bioprosthetic aortic valve (green arrow). B: TEE images show that the vegetation (blue arrow) is located just at the ventricular side of the aortic valve bioprosthesis with subsequent perforation of the anterior mitral valve. There is also thickening of the aortomitral continuity (red arrow) suggestive of abscess due to endocarditis."
